invariant: INV-7
file: quic_version.h
catches: quic_test
reason: version 2 derives its packet protection key, IV and header
  protection key under version 1's labels, where RFC 9369 section 3.3.2
  names "quicv2 key", "quicv2 iv" and "quicv2 hp" (rfc9369.txt:167-174),
  so every version 2 packet at every level is protected under keys no
  version 2 peer holds. test/quic_version2_tests.h requires RFC 9369
  Appendix A.1's keys and the HkdfLabel bytes it prints, and A.5's key,
  IV and header protection key.

--- old
        {"quicv2 key", "quicv2 iv", "quicv2 hp", "quicv2 ku"},
--- new
        {"quic key", "quic iv", "quic hp", "quicv2 ku"},
